---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Terms" description="Terms for using this site and, if we work together, how proposals, invoices and payments work." currentNav="">
  <div class="page-fade site-frame">
    <div class="hero">
      <div class="label"><div class="eyebrow">terms</div></div>
      <div>
        <h1>Terms</h1>
        <p class="lede">Updated 2026-10-10. Short and plain: how you may use what is published here, and the default terms if you hire me.</p>

        <h2>Content</h2>
        <p>Essays and notes are published under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CC BY 4.0</a>: reuse them with attribution and a link. Code in linked repositories follows each repository's own license.</p>
        <p>Everything here is my personal opinion and general information. It is not financial, legal or investment advice, and it does not speak for any employer or client.</p>

        <h2>Working together</h2>
        <p>Consulting and advisory work starts with a written proposal (email is enough) stating scope, timeline and price. The engagement starts when you accept it in writing. If a signed proposal or contract says something different from this page, the proposal wins.</p>

        <h2>Invoices and payment</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Prices are in the currency stated in the proposal and exclude taxes unless stated otherwise.</li>
          <li>Invoices carry the legal details required where they are issued.</li>
          <li>Unless agreed otherwise, payment is by bank transfer within 15 days of the invoice date.</li>
          <li>Retainers are invoiced in advance at the start of each period. If an invoice is more than 30 days overdue, work may pause after written notice.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Cancellation</h2>
        <p>Retainers can be cancelled with 30 days' written notice. Project work is invoiced for what was done up to cancellation. Payments for periods already delivered are not refunded.</p>

        <h2>Confidentiality and data</h2>
        <p>What you share for the work stays confidential. If it includes personal data, I process it only for the agreed work and on your instructions.</p>

        <h2>Liability</h2>
        <p>Except for wilful misconduct or gross negligence, total liability for an engagement is limited to the fees paid for it in the last 3 months, and there is no liability for lost profits or indirect damages.</p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>Each engagement is governed by the law named in its proposal or contract. If none is named, the law of the place where the invoice is issued applies.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p><a href="https://github.com/xronocode" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/xronocode</a> · <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/xronocode" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  h2 { margin: 28px 0 8px; }
  p, li { max-width: 62ch; }
  p { margin: 0 0 12px; }
  ul { margin: 0 0 12px; padding-left: 1.2em; }
  li { margin: 4px 0; }
  p a { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
</style>
